\section{Verification and cross-checks}\label{sec:verif}
% ===========================================================================
\texttt{ionization\_yield.py} runs 50 checks and prints per-check coverage
rather than a verdict tally. The ones that carry weight:

\begin{table}[h]\centering\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}llp{7.2cm}@{}}
\toprule
ID & Check & Outcome \\
\midrule
C32 & \textbf{SvdS coefficients} & recalled vs \cite{fs10} eq.~(13):
     $0.001764$\src{svds\_vs\_fs10\_ion\_reldiff} relative; vs eq.~(14):
     $0.01101$\src{svds\_vs\_fs10\_heat\_reldiff}. First external test they have had. \\
C32 & \cite{fs10} footnote 8 & the recalled heating fit sits $4.6\%$ absolute above the
     SvdS exact $0.32$ at $x_i=0.01$; \cite{fs10} say $\sim6\%$. The known offset is
     reproduced, not removed. \\
C32 & \textbf{eq.~(2) medians} & computed $7.356$\src{fs10\_median\_secondary\_HI\_eV},
     $14.51$, $\SI{29.89}{\electronvolt}$ against the $7.2$, $14.2$,
     $\SI{28.5}{\electronvolt}$ \cite{fs10} quote: $2.2\%$, $2.2\%$, $4.9\%$. The
     medians are not used to build $p(\varepsilon)$. \\
C32 & External anchor: $W$ & $E_{\rm th}/f_{\rm ion} = \SI{36.26}{\electronvolt}$
     asymptotically against the measured $W(\mathrm{H})\approx\SI{36}{\electronvolt}$. \\
C20 & \textbf{Independent bound} & the eq.~(2) ionization-only cascade gives one pair per
     $\SI{17.93}{\electronvolt}$\src{W\_ion\_only\_eV}, monotone, under $E/E_{\rm th}$, and
     above model~(A) everywhere. Uses no SvdS input. \\
C20 & STRUCTURAL & $dN^{(A)}/dE$ collapses to $f_{\rm ion}/E_{\rm th}$ \emph{exactly} when
     $f_{\rm ion}$ is made constant, so the change in the answer is physics, not
     refactoring. \\
C36 & \textbf{$W(K_e)$ vs constant $W$} & $4.575\times10^{6}$\src{N\_e\_C\_1e+12} against
     $5.059\times10^{6}$\src{N\_e\_C\_1e12\_constW}: a reduction of
     $0.0956$\src{ic\_W\_energy\_dependence\_reduction}. \\
C26 & Platzman budget & $\sum f_i = 0.9600$\src{f\_budget\_sum} $\le1$. \\
C26 & IC spectrum & $\int 3F\,dx = 1$, $\int x\,3F\,dx = 1/3$ to $10^{-12}$. \\
C31 & $\langle w\rangle$ two ways & numeric vs $(\pi^4/15)/(6\zeta(3))$: $10^{-14}$. \\
C31 & $N_{\rm secondary}$ two ways & trapezoid vs adaptive \texttt{quad}: $10^{-6}$. \\
C18 & Structural $A\!\equiv\!0$ / $A\!\equiv\!1$ & zero absorption collapses (C) onto (B)
     \emph{exactly}; full absorption recovers model~(A) and stays under $E/E_{\rm th}$. \\
C20 & Hard ceiling & $N^{(C)}\le E/E_{\rm th}$ everywhere. \\
C53 & Null tests & $N_\gamma=0$ exactly below \SI{13.6}{\electronvolt}; $N_\gamma=1$
     exactly up to \SI{41.6}{\electronvolt}. The plateau edge \emph{moved} when $W(K_e)$
     replaced the constant, and the check is written against the model, not the number. \\
C36 & Sub-100 eV secondaries & $0.2297$\src{ic\_frac\_of\_secondary\_below\_100eV} of the
     secondary yield is made below \SI{100}{\electronvolt}. Suppressing that band gives
     $4.244\times10^{6}$\src{N\_e\_C\_1e12\_pe\_floor\_100eV}, i.e.\ $-7.2\%$. \emph{Reported,
     not resolved.} \\
C36 & Sensitivity: transport & Hubble length vs redshifting light cone,
     $4.575\times10^{6}$\src{N\_e\_C\_1e+12} vs
     $4.339\times10^{6}$\src{N\_e\_C\_1e12\_cosmo}, spread
     $0.0516$\src{ic\_transport\_spread\_max}. \\
C18 & Deliberate failure & a wrong $f_{\rm ion}$ is rejected by the $W$ test; the naive
     linear-space integrator is caught returning
     $0.569$\src{naive\_integral\_fraction} of the correct integral. \\
C56 & Determinism & \texttt{results.json} regenerates byte-identically:
     \texttt{md5} \texttt{270ee358da144c1751517e88b8aa4251} on two independent runs.
     This is a claim about \emph{two} runs, so the script does not assert it --- it
     publishes the hash and leaves the comparison to be made. It had been sitting in
     the automatic tier mislabelled. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\paragraph{Three bugs this suite caught, in this revision alone.} (i) The
linear-space quadrature of Eq.~\eqref{eq:modelB}, whose integrand lives in the
first $10^{-4}$ of the range, returned a value that was wrong \emph{and smooth};
the monotonicity check caught it. (ii) \cite{fs10} eq.~(14) has a different
functional form from eq.~(13); using the eq.~(13) form for heating gave $0.638$
instead of $0.362$, a factor $1.8$, and looked perfectly plausible --- the
comparison against \cite{fs10}'s own quoted $0.32$ caught it. (iii) The cascade
recursion of Eq.~\eqref{eq:cascade} was marched on a logarithmic grid, where
$E-E_{\rm th}-\varepsilon$ falls into the cell that is still empty; it collapsed
from $Y(10^3)=55$ to $Y(10^4)=2.7$, and the monotonicity check caught that too.
A linear grid with step $\ll E_{\rm th}$ makes the march exact.

